                <pb facs="0124" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0046B/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-05T21:00:00+02:00">May 5, 1943—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 5—5:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3130. Department’s 2804, May 4, 3 p.m. Our need for a Consulate at Bahrein was
                    taken up again with Foreign Office in considerable detail on April 12. Foreign
                    Office promptly consulted with Government of India once more. As no reply was
                    forthcoming Foreign Office 2 days ago urged Government of India to expedite its
                    reply. We were assured at Foreign Office today that it will give us an answer
                    just as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
